From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:47:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] avfilter/vf_dovi_reshape: add a profile 8.1 RPU output mode

Add the rpu option. The default, strip, keeps today's behaviour and
removes the Dolby Vision metadata from the reshaped frames, because the
profile 5 RPU describes the IPT base layer and not the reshaped BT.2020
PQ pixels.

rpu=p81 rewrites the metadata instead to a profile 8.1 RPU that fits
the reshaped signal: identity polynomial mapping on all components, the
profile 8.1 YCbCr to RGB and RGB to LMS coefficients, no residual, and
the dynamic metadata (level 1, 2, 6 and the others) kept. Level 5 blocks
are dropped, as the active area no longer applies after reshaping. The
conversion is a port of p5_to_p81 from dovi_tool 2.3.4 (MIT).

libx265 -dolbyvision 1 then writes a profile 8.1 stream. It needs
mastering display data at open; the input's stream side data passes
through unchanged, and an input without it needs
-x265-params master-display=...

Signed-off-by: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
---
 doc/filters.texi              |  24 ++++++-
 libavfilter/dovi_reshape.c    | 117 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 libavfilter/dovi_reshape.h    |   8 +++
 libavfilter/vf_dovi_reshape.c |  45 ++++++++++---
 4 files changed, 184 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/doc/filters.texi b/doc/filters.texi
index 5dcee2e40e205aad7526c74409e8f71fc9aa913f..dae2ed3c23b0e95dcc25c5e9f9fa8b3684ff9c8d 100644
--- a/doc/filters.texi
+++ b/doc/filters.texi
@@ -12337,7 +12337,29 @@ frame metadata.
 Frames without Dolby Vision metadata, limited range frames, and streams whose RPU
 signals a residual enhancement layer (profile 7) are refused with an error.
 
-The filter has no options.
+@subsection Options
+The filter accepts the following options:
+
+@table @option
+@item rpu
+Set the Dolby Vision RPU processing mode.
+
+It accepts the following values:
+@table @samp
+@item strip
+Remove the Dolby Vision metadata from the output frames. This is the default.
+
+@item p81
+Rewrite the Dolby Vision metadata to profile 8.1, which describes the
+reshaped BT.2020 PQ signal. The raw profile 5 RPU is removed.
+
+Profile 8.1 output is meant for libx265 @code{-dolbyvision 1}.
+libx265 needs mastering display data at open, pass
+@code{-x265-params master-display=...} when the input carries none.
+Level 5 (active area) extension blocks are dropped; dovi_tool documents
+that dropping Level 5 metadata produces spec non-conformant RPUs.
+@end table
+@end table
 
 @subsection Example
 Tone map a profile 5 file to SDR BT.709:
diff --git a/libavfilter/dovi_reshape.c b/libavfilter/dovi_reshape.c
index cb6faa138357736519201eebad3e333106ebff00..772dd818614e33daa360a72ecbb204c4084b193e 100644
--- a/libavfilter/dovi_reshape.c
+++ b/libavfilter/dovi_reshape.c
@@ -199,3 +199,120 @@ void ff_dovi_reshape_pixel(const FFDoviReshape *s, const float ycc[3], float rgb
     for (int c = 0; c < 3; c++)
         rgb[c] = pq_oetf(rgb[c]);
 }
+
